JOIN:will combine two tables with each other and provide the combined result.combine data horizontal,it add the rows based on types of the join we are using.
Join/Inner join: A row in table A looks for matching records/rows in table B if there is no matching, so that data wont make it in final table creted by inner join.
-Returns only rows where the join condition matches in both tables,
Any row from either table without a match is excluded from the result set.
-its a intersection oftwo tables and eleiminate the unmatched rows,helps in efficient retrieval.
-join is same as inner join.
--------------------------------------------------
OUTER JOINS:
--------------------
OUTER JOIN/LEFT OUTER JOIN: Returns all rows from the left table, and the matching rows from the right table; if no match exists, right‑table columns are NULL
RIGHT OUTER JOIN Returns all rows from the right table, and the matching rows from the left table; if no match exists, left‑table columns are NULL
FULL OUTER JOIN: get all records from both table and wheater its matching(satisfy the JOIN condition) or not 
along with null values
 records from both table( if there are rows value in left/right side but no matching or satifying condtion 
 on right  then it will assign NULL at right value vice versa)
